 ## Overview
-Vortex-Net is a method for identifying vortices in volumetric flow data by training a convolutional neural network (CNN) to replicate the classification boundary of the Instantaneous Vorticity Deviation (IVD) criterion [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its parent [Neural Network Volume Classification](5271-neural-network-volume-classification.md) by focusing on specific physical feature extraction (vortex identification) rather than general opacity mapping, and from its sibling [Berenjkoub et al. vortex segmentation](10626-berenjkoub-et-al-vortex-segmentation.md) by relying on labels generated from an existing analytical criterion rather than synthetic ground truth [S1, unofficial].
+Vortex-Net is a method for identifying vortices in volumetric flow data by training a convolutional neural network (CNN) to replicate the classification boundary of the Instantaneous Vorticity Deviation (IVD) criterion [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its parent [Neural Network Volume Classification](5271-neural-network-volume-classification.md) by focusing on specific physical feature extraction rather than general opacity mapping, and from its sibling [Berenjkoub et al. vortex segmentation](10626-berenjkoub-et-al-vortex-segmentation.md) by relying on labels generated from an existing analytical criterion rather than synthetic ground truth [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** Local 3D patches of velocity field data $\mathbf{u} = (u, v, w)$ from the volumetric dataset.
-*   **Output:** A binary classification for each patch indicating whether it contains a vortex (1) or background (0).
